  "evidences": [
    {
      "id": "ev_1",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s1"
      },
      "text": "symantec.com /connect/blogs/taiwan-targeted-new-cyberespionage-back-door-trojan Symantec Official Blog Backdoor.Dripion was custom developed, deployed in a highly targeted fashion, and used command and control servers disguised as antivirus company websites.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_2",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s2"
      },
      "text": "In late August 2015, Symantec identified a previously unknown back door Trojan (Backdoor.Dripion) infecting organizations primarily located in Taiwan, as well as Brazil and the United States.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_5",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s5"
      },
      "text": "These attacks have some links to earlier attacks by a group called Budminer involving the Taidoor Trojan (Trojan.Taidoor).",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_17",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s1"
      },
      "text": "The Dripion back door Trojan Once Dripion is installed, the attacker can access the user’s computer.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_18",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s2"
      },
      "text": "Dripion has the functionally of a back door Trojan, letting attackers upload, download, and steal pre- determined information from the victim, and execute remote commands.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_25",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s1"
      },
      "text": "Additionally, the developer of the Dripion malware used XOR encoding for both the binary configuration file (XOR: 0xA8) as well as network requests with the C&C server (XOR: 0xA3), to make detection more difficult.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_30",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s6"
      },
      "text": "The first piece of evidence pointing towards a link with previous cyberespionage campaigns was the use of the Blugger downloader, which has only been used by a group Symantec calls Budminer.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_31",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s7"
      },
      "text": "This group has used Blugger to distribute its own custom malware known as Taidoor (Trojan.Taidoor).",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_33",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s9"
      },
      "text": "Significantly, this is the first time we have seen Blugger used to deliver malware other than Taidoor.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_34",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s10"
      },
      "text": "One of the Blugger samples associated with Dripion connected with a root domain also used in Taidoor-related activity.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_35",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s11"
      },
      "text": "Both of the URL queries originated from the Blugger downloader which connected to the blog classic-blog.[REDACTED DOMAIN 1].com.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_38",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s1"
      },
      "text": "website (classic-blog.[REDACTED DOMAIN 1].com) but also used the same URL (classic- blog.[REDACTED DOMAIN 1].com /nasyzk/[ENCODED TEXT]) to obtain the encrypted C&C configuration.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_46",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s9"
      },
      "text": "For example the domains hyydn.nortonsoft[.]com and mhysix.mcfeesoft[.]com were both C&C domains used in attacks.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_55",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 6,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p6_s8"
      },
      "text": "Not all of the ties are strong on their own, but together provide a strong case that there is a relationship between the groups targeting Taiwan using Dripion and Taidoor malware.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_56",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 6,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p6_s9"
      },
      "text": "Based on the evidence we have presented Symantec attributed the activity involving the Dripion malware to the Budminer advanced threat group.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_57",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Taiwan-targeted-cyberespionage-Trojan(03-29-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 6,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p6_s10"
      },
      "text": "While we have not seen new campaigns using Taidoor malware since 2014, we believe the Budminer group has changed tactics to avoid detection after being outed publicly in security white papers and blogs over the past few years.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
